## Introduction

In this lab, I worked on reducing lock contention in xv6 by redesigning the memory allocator and buffer cache. The goal was to improve parallelism and make the system more efficient on multi-core machines.

---

## Lab Tasks

### Memory Allocator
I redesigned the memory allocator to use **per-CPU free lists**, each with its own lock. This reduced contention on the `kmem` lock and improved parallelism.

---

### Buffer Cache
I redesigned the buffer cache to use a **hash table** with per-bucket locks. This reduced contention on the `bcache` lock and improved file system performance.

---

## Building and Running xv6

1. **Prerequisites**:  
   - I installed the RISC-V toolchain from [riscv-gnu-toolchain](https://github.com/riscv/riscv-gnu-toolchain).
   - I installed QEMU for RISC-V (`riscv64-softmmu`).

2. **Build xv6**:
   ```bash
   $ make qemu

Testing and Grading
I used kalloctest to test my memory allocator implementation.
I used bcachetest to test my buffer cache implementation.
I ran usertests -q to ensure my changes didn't break other functionality.
